Single-database configuration for Flask.

RENTIO is bootstrapped from an empty PostgreSQL database with
`backend/sql/create_database.sql`. The initial project did not have a core
Alembic revision history; the first revision in `versions/` adds the IA
marketing schema to a database whose core tables already exist.

For a database created from the complete SQL bootstrap, run
`flask --app "app:crear_app()" db upgrade` from `backend` to apply migrations
after the bootstrap revision. The Docker PostgreSQL initialization scripts
record that baseline revision automatically. For an existing database whose
Alembic version is already `20261102_01`, this applies the additive catalog,
property-type, and contract changes without dropping existing data.
Revision `20261111_01` adds Medellín's 16 urban communes to the location catalog.
Locations typed by owners that are not in the official catalog are saved as user-provided
sectors, not represented as official barrios.
